Clip the taskbar only when it overflows

With the magnify (Plank) hover animation the icons at both ends move about a
third of an icon outwards, and the taskbar clipped them in half (seen in the
Raiden OS Dock layout, a dock sized to its icons). Clipping is only needed
while the taskbar scrolls.

--- a/taskbar.js
+++ b/taskbar.js
@@ -166,6 +166,15 @@
       upper = Math.floor(upper)
       scrollview._dtpFadeSize = upper > pageSize ? this._delegate.iconSize : 0
 
+      // The magnify (Plank) animation moves the outer icons a little past the
+      // ends; only a taskbar that overflows and scrolls needs to clip them
+      let overflowing = upper > pageSize
+      let content = scrollview.get_child()
+      if (this.clip_to_allocation != overflowing)
+        this.clip_to_allocation = overflowing
+      if (content && 'clip_to_view' in content && content.clip_to_view != overflowing)
+        content.clip_to_view = overflowing
+
       if (
         this._currentBackgroundColor !==
         panel.dynamicTransparency.currentBackgroundColor
